<title>PORTUGAL: Oporto metro finalists Siemens, S.Costa.</title>
<headline>Oporto metro finalists Siemens, S.Costa.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Empresa do Metro do Porto has chosen two international consortia led by German group Siemens and Portuguese group Soares da Costa as finalists in the public competition to build a 130-billion-escudo urban transport system in Oporto, officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>The two finalists were chosen from four consortia.</p>
<p>Siemens bid in partnership with Portuguese groups Mota &amp; Companhia, Teixeira Duarte and Engil ; and Soares da Costa bid in partnership with ABB-Asea Brown, Assiconstroi and Impregilo.</p>
<p>The other two bidding groups were: GEC Alsthom and Portuguese groups Bento Pedroso Construcoes and Somague; and Spie Batignolles/Ansaldo, Bombardier and Grupo Nelson Quintas.</p>
<p>Empresa do Metro do Porto is expected to choose the winning bidder at the end of the first quarter this year, newspapers have said.</p>
<p>Construction work is due to begin in April 1997 and the metro system should open in 2000.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
